  "family_id": "bridgmanite",
  "cell_contents": "Four formula units on the conventional 20-atom Pbnm EOS volume basis. The source calculations use 80-atom supercells (16 formula units) in three shapes; molar Table 1 volumes are converted to the common Z=4 basis.",
  "symmetry": "ORTHORHOMBIC",
  "space_group": "Pbnm",
  "space_group_number": 62,
  "atom_sites": [],
  "peaks": [],
  "notes": "The six records preserve three source-computed Fe configurations for each spin state. They are deliberately model variants rather than six material identities. The authors choose model 1 for subsequent thermodynamics and find high-spin Fe stable through lower-mantle pressures; low-spin records are metastable computational comparisons.",
  "source": {
    "structure_reference": {
      "authors": ["Metsue", "Tsuchiya"],
      "year": 2012,
      "title": "Thermodynamic properties of (Mg,Fe2+)SiO3 perovskite at the lower-mantle pressures and temperatures: an internally consistent LSDA+U study",
